course: dictionary
lesson: 117
title: Adoptive and family words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Adoptive is an adjective. It describes the parents who adopt a child, the family who chooses to bring a child up as their own. «Adoptive parents are real parents.» The word tells you how the parents came to be the child's family.
explain: Birth parents are the parents a child was born to. Adoptive parents are the parents who bring the child up. Both kinds of parent can love and care for a child. The words around adoptive show you which kind of parent is meant.
explain: Adoptive can also describe a home or a country that you choose and come to belong to. Read the sentence around the word to find out which meaning fits. If you are not sure, ask: is this about parents, or about a place?
fact: Adoptive means describing the family who adopts a child.
fact: «Adoptive» is used for the parents: adoptive mother, adoptive parents.
fact: «Adopted» describes the child, so it is a different word from «adoptive».
fact: Birth parents are the parents a child was born to; adoptive parents are the parents who bring the child up.
fact: Adoptive families can look different from each other, and staring at them is rude.
exercise: «Adoptive parents are real parents.» What does adoptive describe here? | The parents who gave birth to a child | A type of bird | *The parents who adopt a child and bring them up | A kind of weather
exercise: Ella says her new country is her adoptive country. What does she mean? | A country that is very cold | A country with no people in it | *A country she chose and came to belong to | A country she was born in
exercise: Find the adjective in this sentence: «Her adoptive mother read to her every night.» | *adoptive | night | read | mother
test: Which word is used for the parents a child was born to? | Gentle | Adopted | Adoptive | *Birth
test: «A calm, proud answer can stop a cruel comment.» Which word describes the family who brings a child up by adopting them? | Cruel | Calm | *Adoptive | Birth
exam: Which word describes the parents who chose to bring a child up as their own? | barely | *adoptive | cuddly | birth
